From df29c7ed195fa993ba12dff302879b0d9effba68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 13:24:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Unify curated templates and tenant style profiles behind
 one picker
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A template is a format, never a video: overlay geometry, caption treatment,
beat rhythm, the structural arc. The tenant always brings the content. If a
template carried content, every workspace would ship the same video, which
social platforms punish and audiences spot immediately.

That makes a curated template and a workspace's own style profile the same
object with different owners, so they share `video_style_profiles` rather than
becoming two half-features that drift. `tenantId` is now nullable, `scope`
says which kind a row is, and the existing list endpoint returns a workspace's
own rows plus every published platform template. One picker, one shape, one
code path.

The rule the new module exists to enforce: a platform template may never
reference a tenant's assets. characterId, brandKitId, styleProfileId and every
/objects/<tenantId>/ path are meaningless in another workspace, and a stale one
either 404s or points at somebody else's file. `TemplateJobDefaults` is typed as
Omit<VideoJobOptions, ...those keys>, so the mistake cannot be written; the
runtime `assertTemplateSafe` catches rows that arrived from the database, where
no type protects them.

On the list path an unsafe curated row is dropped and logged rather than
thrown, so one bad row hides itself instead of taking the whole picker down.
Deletion needed no guard: the route already filters on tenantId, and NULL =
value is never true in Postgres, so a tenant cannot delete a platform row.

Templates declare SLOTS the tenant fills — script, presenter take, brand kit —
and the picker shows them before selection. A card that looks free and then
demands a shoot is the worst possible ordering, since the tenant has already
committed by the time they find out. The presenter slot carries the framing
constraint that actually bites: head and shoulders in the lower two-thirds,
because the overlay occupies the top of the frame and selfie-close footage puts
a graphic across the speaker's face. That is the bug the sample video hit.

estimateVideoUnits puts a run's cost on the card. shotCount drives the funding
reservation, so a template quietly costing eight units every run generates
support tickets. Display only — the charge is still computed from engine and
options at enqueue.

Schema changes are additive and widening: nullable tenantId, new columns with
defaults. No data loss, no backfill.

24 tests. The 31 existing videoStyles and videoGen files still pass.

Follow-up, not built here: superadmin CRUD for curated rows, and the three-tab
picker UI (Curated / Yours / From your best) in the Video Studio. The list
endpoint already returns everything all three tabs need.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
